    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0335" n="323" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/1874: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-15T13:00:00+03:25">May 15, 1942—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 16—8:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>157. Referring to the Department’s No. 116, March 5 [<hi rendition="#italic">May
                        6</hi>], 10 p.m.<anchor n="75" xml:id="d369-f1"/> Minister of War informs me
                    Soviet authorities have given permission for 500 Iranian troops to proceed to
                    Rezaieh area and that they will leave at once. He is endeavoring to obtain
                    permission for additional 1,000 to be sent there.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tabriz.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
